WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.769
-Hey, guys,
we have a big show tonight,

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:05.537
but very big announcement

00:00:05.537 --> 00:00:07.507
to make from T-Mobile.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.175
The last three days
we've asked you to text

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.577
"thanks" to 50555.

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:14.480
T-Mobile said they will match
up to $400,000

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.850
to Girls &amp; Boys Club
of America.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.986
They have a COVID-19
relief fund

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:23.289
for families
that need child care.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.857
So it's a great program.

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:27.793
If you text "thanks," you give
a $5 donation to them,

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:29.529
they will match up to
$400,000.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.430
That's $800,000.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.299
So thank you
for donating to that.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.600
But we have a big
announcement that T-Mobile

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.235
wants to make tonight,

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:39.772
which is very cool
that they're donating --

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:41.674
they're committing
to donating --

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.342
I want to make sure
I get this right --

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:47.913
$2.5 million
to over 100 local schools

00:00:47.913 --> 00:00:49.415
and Boys &amp; Girls Club.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:52.118
That is amazing.
T-Mobile!

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.653
You stepped it up
during this time,

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.554
and that's awesome.
Thank you guys so much.

00:00:55.554 --> 00:00:58.857
I appreciate it.
Now...

00:00:58.857 --> 00:01:00.159
let's start the show.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:02.294
♪♪

00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:03.629
Hi, guys, welcome to

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:05.197
"The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:06.800
My name is Jimmy Fallon.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.768
Thank you so much
for watching all week.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:11.871
I will remind you that next week
we have all new shows as well.

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.741
We have the Jonas Brothers,
L.L. Cool J., Melissa McCarthy,

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:18.111
Octavia Spencer, Halle Berry.
It's going to be giant.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.512
So check out next week,

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.947
all new shows,
all new charities

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:23.248
and stuff to talk about
next week,

00:01:23.248 --> 00:01:24.884
so thank you so much.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:28.621
We have a big show tonight.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.024
Hi. Hi.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.458
We have a big show tonight.

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.594
We have the one and only
Hugh Jackman

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.295
is on the show tonight.

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:39.632
Actors Fund is his charity
he's going with.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.167
We also have Rose Byrne.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:46.672
Her charity is foodbanknyc.org.

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.540
And Bobby Cannavale
actually shows up

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.842
in her interview as well.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.510
I will say I baked bread
with Hugh Jackman,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:52.878
which I'd never done.

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:55.081
It was pretty fun, and I have
the scar to prove it.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:58.384
That was my little battle scar
from baking with Hugh Jackman.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:01.053
Yeah. And then --
But Rose Byrne makes a cocktail

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:03.990
using -- you know those syringes
that come with Baby Advil?

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.259
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:09.829
I've never seen
anything like it. It's great.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:12.865
Also, we have Kesha,
who we would just love, Kesha.

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:16.035
And here is her charity,
to raise money for Crew --

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.070
Live Nation for crew members
out there

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:21.307
that aren't working right now
because of this pandemic.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.976
And then we have another
issue of --

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:25.211
another edition

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.079
of "The Longest Days
of Our Lives."

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:28.948
-[ Gasps ]
-That soap opera that is set

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.383
in quarantine over Zoom

00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:33.452
with people that look
like Kristen Wiig,

00:02:33.452 --> 00:02:35.321
Will Ferrell,
and a very special guest

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.689
that I won't tell you
who it is.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:39.558
Okay. It's Matthew McConaughey.
Because why not?

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:41.127
Why not tell you
who at this point?

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:44.630
Come on. You want -- okay, guys.
You ready for this?

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.465
We're gonna do some
"Thank You Notes."

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:48.601
And then we're gonna do
the monologue.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.136
Well, let's do
the monologue first.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:51.671
Oh, and then before
I even get to the monologue,

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:55.574
I do want to mention lastly,
tomorrow night, the big event,

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:57.777
"One World: At Home Together."

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:01.246
This is with Stephen Colbert,
Jimmy Kimmel and I

00:03:01.246 --> 00:03:02.348
are hosting it.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:05.417
Lady Gaga
headed this whole thing up.

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:06.819
Paul McCartney's
doing something.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:09.755
Elton John. There's certain
names I can't tell you.

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:10.890
Can I say the Rolling Stones?

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.258
I think I can say
the Rolling Stones.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.260
It's out now. The Rolling Stones
are going to be on it.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:17.597
It's two hours of amazing stuff.
Just watch it, enjoy.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.365
Set your DVRs now.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.766
Pause this and set your DVRs

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:23.036
to tape that -- "One World:
Together at Home."

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:25.004
Is that what I said? I might
have said "At Home Together."

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.606
"Together at Home"
is what it is.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.107
Okay. Here we go, guys.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:31.343
Let's start with some monologue.
You ready for monologue jokes?

00:03:31.343 --> 00:03:33.780
-[ Spitting noise ]
-Here we go. Ready?

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.715
Hey, wait, guys, ready for this?

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:38.183
Listen, listen up. Here we go.

00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:39.351
-Hey, you excited?
Yeah.

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:41.321
-Yeah.
-Okay, good.

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:43.389
Welcome to "Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:46.192
Guys, I saw that today
is Bat Appreciation Day.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:48.060
-[ Giggles ]
-Bats are incredible animals.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.695
They can see in the dark.
-Whoa.

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:52.331
-They can use echolocation
to find food.

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:55.367
The only thing they can't do
right now is read the room.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:58.804
-[ Chuckles ]

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:00.840
-That's right.
It's Bat Appreciation Day.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.675
Man, out of all the events
that have been canceled

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.343
in the last month,
you'd have to think that

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:06.411
this might have been
one of them, right?

00:04:06.411 --> 00:04:09.348
-[ Chattering ]

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:11.684
-Guys, I saw that --

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.285
I saw the Dr. Phil
is in hot water

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:16.288
for some comments
he made about the coronavirus.

00:04:16.288 --> 00:04:17.690
You can tell Dr. Phil's
in trouble

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.891
because you just booked
a one-hour

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.659
exclusive interview
with himself.

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:21.894
-You can't!
-Why?

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:24.630
-"Do you feel any remorse?"
"Yes, I do."

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.165
Hey, guys, shh.
Whisper for a second.

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:28.367
Whisper, I'm doing this, okay?
Whisper while I'm doing this.

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.102
Okay? Thank you.

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:38.044
-[ Whispering ]

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:49.255
[ Whispering continues ]

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:51.023
-Listen to this.
I read that many Americans

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:53.559
have tried cutting their
own bangs.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:54.927
Cutting your own bangs
is a great idea

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:56.762
if you ever looked at
Mark Zuckerberg and thought,

00:04:56.762 --> 00:05:00.099
"I want that."

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.467
I've seen some articles

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.269
that offer alternatives
to shaking hands,

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:05.604
like raising your
eyebrows and smiling.

00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:07.139
It was a good idea right up
until the moment

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:10.476
my plumber thought
I was hitting on him.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.311
"How you doing?"

00:05:12.311 --> 00:05:13.979
Listen to this, since
New York streets

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:15.181
are pretty much empty,

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.883
speeding tickets
have nearly doubled.

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.884
On the bright side, most
New Yorkers have appreciated

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:20.819
getting a ticket,
saying it was just nice to yell

00:05:20.819 --> 00:05:23.022
at a stranger again.

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.823
I'm excited about this.
The NFL Draft

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:26.692
is less than a week away.

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:28.527
Yep, the country's
top college football players

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:32.031
will sign multimillion dollar
contracts,

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:35.001
then just keep living
at home with their parents.

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:38.437
And finally, I read that --
you're leaving, too?

00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:40.173
Yeah, might as well.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.241
I read that experts
say coronavirus stress

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.376
could lead to weight gain.

00:05:44.376 --> 00:05:46.078
I think that's what they said.
It was tough to hear

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:48.881
over the sound of my Dorito
and Captain Crunch sandwich.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:50.550
That's our monologue,
everybody.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.818
Now it's time
for "Thank You Notes."

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:54.487
Guys, come on back.

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:58.190
♪♪

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.558
Guys, today is Friday.
♪♪

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:00.759
That's usually when I write out
some thank-you notes

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:02.294
and I send them out
to my friends.

00:06:02.294 --> 00:06:04.430
So if you guys wouldn't mind,
I'd like to write out my weekly

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.932
thank-you notes right now.

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:07.132
You guys want to help?
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:07.132 --> 00:06:09.001
-Cool.
All right. Here we go.

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:11.103
This first one goes --
Music.

00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:14.406
♪♪
Next.

00:06:14.406 --> 00:06:17.176
Thank you, Yeezy Slides,

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:20.813
for looking more like Crocs
than Crocs.

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:23.482
'Cause they look like
a crocodile to you.

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:25.250
All right, next one.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:27.753
-[ Whispering ]

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:31.590
-Next, next one, yeah.
-Mm.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:32.824
-Music.
♪♪

00:06:32.824 --> 00:06:35.127
Thank you,
smudgy webcam lens,

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:38.663
for being my soft focus
beauty secret on Zoom.

00:06:38.663 --> 00:06:40.733
♪♪
Next one.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.168
♪♪

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:45.137
Thank you, new Drake song,
"Toosie Slide,"

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:47.272
for giving dads
super specific instructions

00:06:47.272 --> 00:06:50.076
on how to embarrass their kids
on TikTok.

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:52.712
Right foot up,
left foot slide!

00:06:52.712 --> 00:06:55.614
Here comes Dad,
shaking his behind!

00:06:55.614 --> 00:06:58.517
♪♪

00:06:58.517 --> 00:07:01.921
-[ Makes spitting noise,
giggles ]

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.589
[ Giggling ]

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:08.160
♪♪

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.796
[ Music stops ]

00:07:10.796 --> 00:07:13.298
[ Music resumes ]

00:07:13.298 --> 00:07:15.234
[ Music stops ]

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.970
[ Music resumes ]

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.939
Thank you, reports that
the SATs and ACTs

00:07:20.939 --> 00:07:24.142
might be canceled this year
because of the coronavirus.

00:07:24.142 --> 00:07:25.845
Or as Scantron put it,

00:07:25.845 --> 00:07:28.548
[ Robotic voice ]
"What is my purpose now?"

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:31.583
-Next one.

00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:34.486
[ Music fades ]

00:07:34.486 --> 00:07:38.090
-Music. Thank you --
[ Music stops and starts ]

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.893
Thank you, mirrors, for that
brief moment of thinking,

00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:45.064
"Hey, someone new to talk to.
Oh, that's just me."

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:47.699
-[ Chuckles ]
-Next.

00:07:47.699 --> 00:07:49.434
Did you laugh at that one?

00:07:49.434 --> 00:07:51.470
-Mm.
-You did? No?

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:53.339
No, you didn't.

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:56.642
Thank you, lines where everyone
is standing six feet apart,

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:59.444
for looking like a drive-thru
where the cars are invisible.

00:07:59.444 --> 00:08:01.314
[ Giggling ]
-Next?

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:03.683
-Yeah.

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:05.951
Okay.

00:08:05.951 --> 00:08:08.053
Music, please.

00:08:08.053 --> 00:08:09.988
♪♪

00:08:09.988 --> 00:08:12.825
Thank you, a glass of wine
before going to bed,

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:15.227
